      {
        "id": 57418,
        "name": "Koey",
        "username": "Koey",
        "avatar_template": "/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/koey/{size}/2187_2.png",
        "created_at": "2013-04-05T02:32:51.000Z",
        "cooked": "<aside class=\"quote group-playtesters\" data-username=\"Spiff\">\n<div class=\"title\">\n<div class=\"quote-controls\"></div>\n<img loading=\"lazy\" alt=\"\" width=\"24\" height=\"24\" src=\"https://forums.greaterthangames.com/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/spiff/48/1865_2.png\" class=\"avatar\"> Spiff:</div>\n<blockquote>\n<p>Yeah, sux. &nbsp;Legacy will almost never benefit from his own Galvanization because it gets turned on in the Power phase (after he's played any one-shots) and turned off in the Start phase (before he plays any one-shots or powers).</p>\n</blockquote>\n</aside>\n<p>With Legacy ring you can still play Galvanize, then Motivational Charge. Or have Omnitron or Agent Adept let you play out of turn.</p>\n<p>So I wouldn't say never <img src=\"https://forums.greaterthangames.com/images/emoji/apple/slight_smile.png?v=12\" title=\":slight_smile:\" class=\"emoji\" alt=\":slight_smile:\" loading=\"lazy\" width=\"20\" height=\"20\"></p>",
        "post_number": 23,
        "post_type": 1,
        "updated_at": "2021-02-07T02:32:44.806Z",
